<!--
  ============================================================================
  JawaCombatViability_Tuning.xml             Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-11
  ============================================================================

  THE OBSERVATION
  ===============
  Observed in-game 2026-08-11, during the ion blaster acceptance test: a Jawa
  fainted in the middle of a firefight.

  THE CAUSE
  =========
  BTD_Jawa carries Turn_Gene_Terrified, from Integrated Genes
  (turnovus.biotech.integratedgenes, load 180). Its own description:

      "Carriers of this gene have an overactive fight-or-flight response...
       They can't even handle basic combat without becoming overwhelmed
       and fainting."
      customEffectDescriptions:
        "May have a fainting spell while in combat."
        "Fainting frequency depends on surrounding terror level."

      geneClass      IntegratedGenes.Gene_Terrified
      mentalBreakDef Turn_MentalBreak_TerrifiedFaintingSpell
      statFactors    Terror x1.5
      biostatMet     +2
      displayCategory Turn_GeneCategory_Slavery

  This is not a bug. It is the gene working exactly as designed, and as
  flavour it is close to perfect — canon Jawa are famously cowardly and flee
  rather than fight. The problem is purely that OUR COLONISTS ARE ALL JAWA.
  A colony that faints when attacked cannot defend the gravship.

  ⚠️ IT GETS WORSE OVER TIME, NOT BETTER. Fainting frequency scales with the
  surrounding Terror level, and the gene multiplies Terror by 1.5. Terror comes
  from corpses, prisoners and slaves — and this is a slaver campaign
  (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/jawa_society.md §4). So the exact conditions the campaign is
  built around are the conditions that make this gene fire most often. It would
  have degraded steadily and looked like a difficulty curve rather than a gene.

  WHY A SWAP, NOT A REMOVAL
  =========================
  First pass here simply deleted the gene. That was the wrong shape. A sweep of
  every gene in the active load set that mentions Terror or fainting found no
  milder sibling to swap in…

      Turn_Gene_Terrified   Terror x1.5   met +2   break = TerrifiedFaintingSpell
      Turn_Gene_FreeSpirit  Terror x0.2   met +1   break = FreeSpiritRampage
      FireTerror            (pyrophobia, unrelated)

  — but "no existing gene fits" is not the same as "the choice is binary". We
  can author one, and that is the better answer: keep the flavour, drop the
  incapacitation. See Defs/GeneDefs/JawaSkittish.xml.

  WHY NOT PATCH Turn_Gene_Terrified ITSELF
  ========================================
  It is used by exactly four xenotypes in this load set:

      guy762_xenotype_jawa        guy762_xenotype_nemoidian
      BTD_Jawa                    BTD_Neimoidian

  Jawa and Neimoidians. Softening the shared gene would also flatten the Trade
  Federation, who are NPC-only and whose fainting costs the player nothing and
  is quietly delightful. So the original gene is left completely untouched and
  only BTD_Jawa is re-pointed.

  ⚠️ COST: the donor is worth +2 biostatMet, the replacement +1, so BTD_Jawa
  ends up one metabolism poorer. In Biotech's economy a drawback pays the
  xenotype, and most of the drawback is now gone — claiming the full +2 would
  be quietly buying a free point. Deliberately NOT compensating elsewhere;
  rebalancing BTD_Jawa's totals is a decision for
  design/Jawa/worldbuilding/jawa_society.md, not for a mechanism patch.

  SAFETY AND LOAD ORDER
  =====================
  PatchOperationConditional on the exact <li>, so it is a silent no-op if
  Xenotype REMIX ever drops the gene itself. BTD_Jawa is defined by Xenotype
  REMIX at load 555 and Jawa_Patches is 564, so the def exists when we patch it.

  The xpath uses a text() predicate, which RimWorld's XPath supports but
  validate_patch.py cannot evaluate — it will report UNSUPPORTED rather than a
  hit count. Verified by hand against the resolved load set 2026-08-11: the
  gene is present in BTD_Jawa's <genes> list.

  VERIFY AFTER THE NEXT LOAD
  ==========================
    * A fresh Jawa's gene list shows "skittish", not "terrified".
    * Start a firefight; no fainting spells.
    * Expect the xenotype's metabolism total to read 1 lower than before.
    * Spawn a Neimoidian: it should STILL have "terrified".
  ============================================================================

  🔴 RETARGETED 2026-08-19 (B58 / btd-jawa-has-no-merge). Every operation below named
  `BTD_Jawa`, and that def NO LONGER LOADS — measured against the live def dump, where
  the surviving Jawa xenotypes are `MandrakeJawa` (35 genes, the owner's hand-built set
  and by `ideoligion/APPROVED.md` the ONLY active one) and `RimMandrakeJawa` (24,
  generator output). Every op was matching zero and doing nothing.
  ⭐ They are retargeted rather than deleted, and they are all no-ops TODAY: `MandrakeJawa`
  already satisfies all six conditions. They stay as the guard that keeps the ratified
  appearance and viability decisions true if the xenotype is ever regenerated from the
  `.xtp` and loses one.
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- ==================================================================
       1. Drop the fainting gene from Jawa (left intact for Neimoidians)
       ================================================================== -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="MandrakeJawa"]/genes/li[text()="Turn_Gene_Terrified"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
      <xpath>/Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="MandrakeJawa"]/genes/li[text()="Turn_Gene_Terrified"]</xpath>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- ==================================================================
       2. Put our own skittish gene in its place
       ================================================================== -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="MandrakeJawa"]/genes[not(li[text()="RimMandrake_Jawa_Skittish"])]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="MandrakeJawa"]/genes[not(li[text()="RimMandrake_Jawa_Skittish"])]</xpath>
      <value>
        <li>RimMandrake_Jawa_Skittish</li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
